# Cursor Updates

## Fix for Numeric Topic Hashtag Matching

### Summary
Fixed verify-live script failure for posts with numeric topic keywords like "360". The verification gate was rejecting valid posts because the hashtag matcher only recognized hashtags starting with letters.

### Root Cause
Posts with numeric keywords like "360" (Public 360 software) generate hashtags like #360. The live HTML correctly contained these hashtags, but the verification regex required hashtags to start with a letter. This caused deployments to fail even though the site was correctly deployed.

### Changes Made
Updated firstHtmlHashtags function in scripts/verify-live.mjs to match hashtags starting with either letters or numbers, while filtering out 6-digit and 8-digit hex color codes.

Added comprehensive test coverage for numeric hashtags and hex color filtering.

### Technical Details
Changed regex from letter-only start to alphanumeric start
Added post-match filtering to exclude 6-digit hex colors like #0F1117
Added post-match filtering to exclude 8-digit hex colors like #AABBCCDD
Retained matching for 3-digit numbers like #360 as valid topics

### Testing
All existing tests pass
New test case for #360 hashtag matching
New test case for hex color exclusion
Lint and build successful

